    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm not sure I follow that \"innovation system tax\" part. What I mean is, if I have to pay my staff significantly more, my profit margins are going to shrink. Some people say that's just the price of having a decent workforce and helping the local economy, but it feels like it's being forced on small owners who are already struggling. Is there actually any data showing that a higher minimum wage doesn't just end up hurting local shops like mine by forcing us to raise prices or cut staff?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
